{"name":"Skipping Rocks","hex":"#d1d0c9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"skipping","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of skip"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act by which something is skipped or omitted.","The game, activity, or exercise of jump rope."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skipping"},{"term":"rocks","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of rock"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Money.","Testicles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rocks"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stone skipping","blocks":[{"text":"Stone skipping and stone skimming are the arts of throwing a flat stone across water in such a way that it bounces off the surface. \"Skipping\" counts the number of bounces; \"skimming\" measures the distance traveled."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Stone_skimming_-Patagonia-9Mar2010.jpg/330px-Stone_skimming_-Patagonia-9Mar2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_skipping"},{"title":"Rock (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rock is any naturally occurring solid mass or aggregate of minerals or mineraloid matter. It is categorized by the minerals included, its chemical composition, and the way in which it is formed. Rocks form the Earth's outer solid layer, the crust, and most of its interior, except for the liquid outer core and pockets of magma in the asthenosphere. The study of rocks involves multiple subdisciplines of geology, including petrology and mineralogy. It may be limited to rocks found on Earth, or it may include planetary geology that studies the rocks of other celestial objects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg/330px-Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thum